 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "The comparison morphism of sites",
 "statement": "For a scheme $T$, the inclusion of etale $T$-schemes into weakly etale\n$T$-schemes is continuous and preserves finite limits. It defines a geometric\nmorphism\n\n$$\n \\nu_T:T_{\\Proet}\\longrightarrow T_{\\Et},\n \\qquad\n \\nu_T^*:\\Sh(T_{\\Et})\\rightleftarrows\n \\Sh(T_{\\Proet}):\\nu_{T,*}.\n$$\n\nFor a finite discrete ring $\\Lambda$, the same adjunction acts on sheaves of\n$\\Lambda$-modules.",
 "source": {
